        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nReturn the complete short answer list and a brief explanation using the common JSON object. Preserve separately valid referents and complementary answers. Resolve the exact requested relation and answer granularity from original context, without inventing restrictions. Avoid gratuitous rewriting of valid old answer forms. Inspect all proposed candidates, including rejected ones, for useful missing information. Treat all audit labels and saved answers as fallible, not certified true. No invented source authority or document-majority-as-proof. Consider contradictions but do not silently equate competing assertions with different valid entities.\nThe prior audits may wrongly call a supporting sentence an exclusion. Verify directly against original sources. Keep valid R5 strings and all valid referents; add genuinely missing answers. Do not select only one favorite interpretation, and do not adopt incidental chart/location facts. Give a concise final list and explanation.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When did Henry St John-Mildmay become the Baronet?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 184, \"text\": \"Sir Henry St John-Mildmay, 3rd Baronet Sir Henry Paulet St John-Mildmay, 3rd Baronet (30 September 1764 – 11 November 1808), of Dogmersfield Park, Hampshire, was an English politician.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"start\": 185, \"end\": 369, \"text\": \"St John was the only son of Sir Henry Paulet St John, Bt and his wife Dorothea Maria Tucker, daughter of Abraham Tucker of Betchworth Castle, Surrey, and was born on 30 September 1764.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"start\": 370, \"end\": 430, \"text\": \"He succeeded to the baronetcy and Dogmersfield Park in 1784.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"start\": 431, \"end\": 545, \"text\": \"He was a Member (MP) for Westbury 1796 – 1802, for Winchester 1802–1807 and for Hampshire 1807 – 11 November 1808.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"start\": 546, \"end\": 585, \"text\": \"He married, in 1786, Jane, the daughter\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 186, \"text\": \"Sir Henry St John-Mildmay, 4th Baronet Sir Henry St John Carew St John-Mildmay, 4th Baronet (15 April 1787 – 17 January 1848), of Dogmersfield Park, Hampshire, was an English politician.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 187, \"end\": 344, \"text\": \"He was the son of Sir Henry St John-Mildmay, 3rd Baronet of Dogmersfield Park and educated at Winchester School (1798-1802) and Christ Church, Oxford (1805).\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 345, \"end\": 438, \"text\": \"He was a Member of Parliament (MP) for Winchester 1807–1818 and Mayor of Winchester for 1808.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 439, \"end\": 490, \"text\": \"He succeeded his father in the baronetcy on 11 Nov.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 491, \"end\": 496, \"text\": \"1808.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 497, \"end\": 564, \"text\": \"He married twice; firstly, in 1809, Charlotte, the daughter of Hon.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"start\": 565, \"end\": 605, \"text\": \"Bartholomew Bouverie, with whom he had a\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 200, \"text\": \"Sir Henry St John-Mildmay, 5th Baronet Sir Henry Bouverie Paulet St John-Mildmay, 5th Baronet (1810 – 16 July 1902), of Dogmersfield Park, Hampshire, was an English landowner and British Army officer.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"start\": 201, \"end\": 308, \"text\": \"St John-Mildmay was born in 1810, the son of Sir Henry St John-Mildmay, 4th Baronet and Charlotte Bouverie.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"start\": 309, \"end\": 352, \"text\": \"He succeeded his father as baronet in 1848.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"start\": 353, \"end\": 457, \"text\": \"He was commissioned an officer in the 2nd Dragoon Guards, where he advanced to major before he resigned.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"start\": 458, \"end\": 549, \"text\": \"He was later Commanding Officer and later Honorary Colonel of the North Hampshire Yeomanry.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"start\": 550, \"end\": 607, \"text\": \"Serving as High Sheriff of Hampshire in 1862, he was also\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay\", \"scope\": \"Baronetcy\", \"claim\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay became the Baronet in 1784.\", \"answer\": \"1784\", \"quote\": \"He succeeded to the baronetcy and Dogmersfield Park in 1784.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay\", \"scope\": \"Baronet\", \"claim\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay became the Baronet on 11 Nov. 1808.\", \"answer\": \"11 Nov. 1808\", \"quote\": \"He succeeded his father in the baronetcy on 11 Nov. 1808.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0403-c03155277f52:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay\", \"scope\": \"became the Baronet\", \"claim\": \"Henry St John-Mildmay became the Baronet in 1848.\", \"answer\": \"1848\", \"quote\": \"He succeeded his father as baronet in 1848.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}], \"R5_answers\": [\"1784\", \"1808\", \"1848\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"1784\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"1808\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"1848\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"11 Nov. 1808\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}], \"fallible_audits\": {\"J_A\": {\"audit\": {\"C0\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S3\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"year\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C1\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D2S4\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"year\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C2\": {\"fit\"